WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.644
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:09.914 --> 00:11.950
Don't tell anyone what I'm about to tell you.

3
00:24.496 --> 00:26.631
Can you tell me your story?

4
00:28.733 --> 00:30.869
The security camera footage with me on it…

5
00:32.537 --> 00:34.372
Who in the police has seen it?

6
00:34.439 --> 00:35.540
Your story first.

7
00:35.607 --> 00:36.841
I'll ask again.

8
00:38.710 --> 00:40.712
-Who saw it? -You first--

9
00:40.778 --> 00:43.448
We don't intend to harm you.

10
00:43.515 --> 00:44.782
Please put this on.

11
00:44.849 --> 00:45.917
A blindfold?

12
00:45.984 --> 00:47.018
If you please.

13
00:50.155 --> 00:51.322
Please get in.

14
00:52.223 --> 00:53.258
-Yes. -Really?

15
00:53.791 --> 00:55.560
-Let's go. -Hang on.

16
00:56.227 --> 00:57.595
For real?

17
01:08.306 --> 01:09.908
Maybe one of you should go home.

18
01:09.974 --> 01:12.410
No, I can't leave after coming this far.

19
01:12.477 --> 01:15.113
You're looking for Harune Nikaido, right, insurance man?

20
01:15.180 --> 01:17.148
I'm not an "insurance man." I'm an investigator!

21
01:17.215 --> 01:19.217
Please identify yourselves as well.

22
01:19.284 --> 01:20.818
You're not office workers, right?

23
01:20.885 --> 01:25.023
It would help a lot if you told us where Harune is and what she's doing.

24
01:27.659 --> 01:29.194
Huh? Did time stop?

25
01:31.229 --> 01:33.598
Mr. Monden, are you police?

26
01:34.732 --> 01:36.768
From your eyes and the way you moved.

27
01:36.834 --> 01:38.770
I figured you must be police.

28
01:38.836 --> 01:40.271
Which department?

29
01:45.610 --> 01:47.946
Hokkaido Police HQ, Organized Crime Division.

30
01:48.546 --> 01:49.514
What?

31
01:49.581 --> 01:53.117
-So everyone here is Hokkaido police? -No.

32
01:53.184 --> 01:56.688
She's from the Hokkaido Bureau of Health, Narcotics Control. A narcotics agent.

33
01:56.754 --> 02:00.225
And I'm with Hakodate Customs Anti-Smuggling Department.

34
02:00.291 --> 02:05.163
So, police, narcotics, customs.

35
02:05.230 --> 02:07.332
Is this a joint operation?

36
02:07.899 --> 02:09.033
That is correct.

37
02:09.667 --> 02:12.170
-Show me your IDs. -Now's not the time.

38
02:12.237 --> 02:14.606
They sound fishy. This could be a kind of scam.

39
02:14.672 --> 02:15.673
Give me your phone.

40
02:15.740 --> 02:16.574
Huh?

41
02:16.641 --> 02:18.309
Don't "huh" me. Your phone.

42
02:22.780 --> 02:23.815
Here.

43
02:24.782 --> 02:25.450
You too.

44
02:28.886 --> 02:30.588
But if anything happens to me,

45
02:30.655 --> 02:34.392
my Tokyo investigation report is set to be sent to my station,

46
02:34.459 --> 02:36.828
along with the CCTV footage.

47
02:38.396 --> 02:40.932
I don't know what happened on that mountain…

48
02:40.999 --> 02:42.600
-Undo those settings. -Do it!

49
02:42.667 --> 02:45.837
I'll undo it once I know why you're gathered here.

50
02:46.404 --> 02:48.740
Okay, okay! Stop!

51
02:48.806 --> 02:51.342
Our identities are genuine!

52
02:52.543 --> 02:55.913
We're investigating a certain drug case.

53
02:56.981 --> 02:59.183
We were tracking Motoka Tabatake.

54
03:01.853 --> 03:03.454
Since we're on a drug case,

55
03:03.521 --> 03:06.424
shouldn't we minimize the risk of information leakage?

56
03:06.491 --> 03:09.193
Mr. Ogoma aside, do we need to let Mr. Nao hear this?

57
03:09.260 --> 03:12.397
Because of my job, I bet I'm the best secret keeper around here.

58
03:12.463 --> 03:15.066
I've cooperated with police investigations many times.

59
03:15.133 --> 03:17.235
The investigation of this case--

60
03:17.302 --> 03:18.970
-Whoa! -Hey, you okay?

61
03:19.037 --> 03:20.571
Such a pain. Just leave.

62
03:20.638 --> 03:22.106
What era is he from?

63
03:22.173 --> 03:24.409
-You're the one who got caught! -What?!

64
03:24.475 --> 03:26.978
-You stand out too much! -I know that.

65
03:27.045 --> 03:28.946
Wait, aren't you two married?

66
03:29.013 --> 03:30.415
No!

67
03:33.284 --> 03:35.453
Can I start explaining?

68
03:36.187 --> 03:37.522
Do you need the restroom first?

69
03:37.588 --> 03:38.790
I'll go quickly.

70
03:38.856 --> 03:41.192
-Go ahead. -Please start. Hold it in.

71
03:41.259 --> 03:42.260
How long will it take?

72
03:42.327 --> 03:43.961
Six months ago,

73
03:44.028 --> 03:47.999
a neighboring country sent information to Hakodate Customs.

74
03:48.066 --> 03:51.469
About a certain product being sent to Japan regularly.

75
03:51.536 --> 03:55.306
It contains an essential ingredient for making banned drugs.

76
03:55.373 --> 03:56.407
What product?

77
03:56.474 --> 03:57.909
Which neighboring country?

78
03:57.975 --> 04:00.678
We are only telling you what we can.

79
04:01.212 --> 04:05.183
Dangerous things entering from overseas must be stopped at all costs.

80
04:05.249 --> 04:10.021
If they are used for criminal purposes, it will be Customs' responsibility.

81
04:10.088 --> 04:16.027
We confirmed that Tabatake herself received the package we were tipped about.

82
04:20.531 --> 04:21.866
Yes, she received it.

83
04:21.933 --> 04:25.503
Of course, we also checked the contents ourselves.

84
04:25.570 --> 04:30.141
Customs has investigative authority but no arrest powers,

85
04:32.176 --> 04:34.746
so we asked Narcotics and the police…

86
04:36.347 --> 04:38.116
We joined the investigation.

87
04:38.750 --> 04:39.784
You tell the rest.

88
04:42.053 --> 04:47.091
Tabatake has no prior record in drug smuggling.

89
04:47.892 --> 04:52.196
We figured she couldn't be the endpoint, but just a courier.

90
04:52.263 --> 04:54.565
So we monitored where the package went.

91
04:55.099 --> 04:56.000
A courier?

92
04:56.067 --> 04:56.968
I love you.

93
04:57.034 --> 04:58.069
I love you.

94
04:58.136 --> 05:01.439
Tabatake received the package,

95
05:01.506 --> 05:04.809
carried it somewhere, and handed it to someone.

96
05:06.244 --> 05:08.913
Finding the delivery destination was difficult.

97
05:08.980 --> 05:12.283
As a mountain guide and a driver,

98
05:12.350 --> 05:15.386
she went all over Hokkaido.

99
05:16.020 --> 05:22.693
But we noticed a pattern in her actions the day after a package was delivered.

100
05:23.661 --> 05:26.230
She always climbed Mt. Shikara.

101
05:26.297 --> 05:29.367
She carried a rather heavy pack for a day trip.

102
05:29.434 --> 05:33.738
In town, we could monitor her, but in the mountains, it's difficult.

103
05:33.805 --> 05:38.042
So we posed as tour guests to watch Tabatake's movements.

104
05:38.109 --> 05:40.611
And find out where the goods went.

105
05:41.379 --> 05:43.381
That was the only way.

106
05:44.081 --> 05:47.585
For a courier, Tabatake lacked wariness.

107
05:47.652 --> 05:51.622
Ms. Saruwatari, you've climbed this mountain several times, right?

108
05:51.689 --> 05:52.590
Yes.

109
05:52.657 --> 05:56.060
"Maybe she isn't carrying the goods today."

110
05:56.127 --> 05:59.630
"Today's operation might come to nothing."

111
05:59.697 --> 06:02.099
Those were the worries we had.

112
06:04.001 --> 06:05.169
Mr. Tsugaru?

113
06:05.937 --> 06:07.138
No.

114
06:10.541 --> 06:11.876
Tsugaru.

115
06:11.943 --> 06:14.645
Tabatake's breathing changed.

116
06:14.712 --> 06:16.180
She was wary of Nikaido.

117
06:16.247 --> 06:17.715
Ring this up please.

118
06:17.782 --> 06:21.752
Tabatake called Nikaido "Tsugaru," right?

119
06:21.819 --> 06:22.854
That's correct.

120
06:22.920 --> 06:25.056
They clearly knew each other.

121
06:25.122 --> 06:28.926
However, Nikaido was not on Tabatake's friend list

122
06:28.993 --> 06:34.265
or her contact list, so we didn't know who he was.

123
06:34.332 --> 06:36.133
Hey, can you take a photo of me?

124
06:36.200 --> 06:37.502
-Is here okay? -Yes!

125
06:41.339 --> 06:42.340
Here I go.

126
06:42.406 --> 06:43.307
Okay.

127
06:43.374 --> 06:45.843
When we asked the police headquarters,

128
06:45.910 --> 06:49.347
we learned he was a man running a restaurant in Asahikawa.

129
06:49.413 --> 06:52.250
If the police know him,

130
06:52.316 --> 06:54.886
does that mean Nikaido had a criminal record?

131
06:55.553 --> 06:58.422
No, he was a witness in a fraud case.

132
06:58.489 --> 06:59.457
A witness?

133
06:59.524 --> 07:02.393
We are only telling you what we can.

134
07:02.460 --> 07:07.465
Nikaido didn't use his real name and approached Tabatake under a false one.

135
07:08.833 --> 07:10.968
We believed there must be a reason,

136
07:11.035 --> 07:14.005
and so we watched their actions and conversations closely.

137
07:14.071 --> 07:16.874
-The pixie-eye primrose. -I see.

138
07:16.941 --> 07:19.544
It's common sense to take trash home with you.

139
07:23.014 --> 07:24.448
Mr. Nikaido.

140
07:24.515 --> 07:27.818
The package delivered to Tabatake weighed two kilograms.

141
07:27.885 --> 07:30.521
If she secretly took it out of her backpack,

142
07:30.588 --> 07:32.890
we could tell by how her steps got lighter.

143
07:32.957 --> 07:35.326
And that would be where she left the goods.

144
07:35.393 --> 07:39.030
Why did Nikaido join the tour?

145
07:39.096 --> 07:42.199
Why did he approach Tabatake?

146
07:42.700 --> 07:43.834
We don't know yet.

147
07:43.901 --> 07:45.903
There is something I would like to show you.

148
07:47.204 --> 07:50.675
None of us could predict that there would be such a thunderstorm.

149
07:51.375 --> 07:54.245
Mr. Monden! Misaki!

150
07:54.312 --> 07:57.014
Mr. Uematsu! Are you hurt?

151
07:57.081 --> 07:59.584
I'm okay!

152
07:59.650 --> 08:00.851
I'm going home.

153
08:00.918 --> 08:01.752
Don't move!

154
08:01.819 --> 08:03.688
I'm cold. A bath…

155
08:03.754 --> 08:06.424
-Mr. Nikaido! -I want to take a bath!

156
08:06.490 --> 08:07.725
Mr. Nikaido!

157
08:07.792 --> 08:09.193
Mr. Nikaido!

158
08:09.260 --> 08:11.829
-It's dangerous! -Are you all right?

159
08:11.896 --> 08:14.665
-Please stay here! -Hey!

160
08:14.732 --> 08:15.933
Help me, you moron!

161
08:16.000 --> 08:19.870
We couldn't follow Tabatake and Nikaido.

162
08:20.471 --> 08:21.839
They got away from us.

163
08:21.906 --> 08:24.575
Who chased Nikaido when he went down?

164
08:24.642 --> 08:26.043
Tabatake.

165
08:26.110 --> 08:29.647
About an hour later, Saruwatari also went down to seek help.

166
08:30.181 --> 08:33.417
And then one died, and two went missing.

167
08:33.484 --> 08:37.254
Even with bad weather, we have to admit the operation failed.

168
08:37.321 --> 08:39.056
-We found a personal item. -Thanks!

169
08:39.123 --> 08:40.858
-We're going home. -See you tomorrow.

170
08:43.094 --> 08:46.530
Who in the police knows you were investigating a drug case?

171
08:46.597 --> 08:49.100
Only the bare minimum.

172
08:49.166 --> 08:50.601
The rescue team…

173
08:50.668 --> 08:52.670
Do you know how hard they searched for you?!

174
08:52.737 --> 08:54.872
The search was called off four days ago.

175
08:55.473 --> 08:57.642
And Tabatake, whom we rescued…

176
08:58.943 --> 08:59.810
She died.

177
08:59.877 --> 09:01.779
Whose fault do you think that was?!

178
09:02.313 --> 09:04.649
She jumped when you looked away?

179
09:04.715 --> 09:07.485
You useless small-town police ruined our investigation!

180
09:07.551 --> 09:09.220
How will you take responsibility?

181
09:09.286 --> 09:10.221
Well?

182
09:12.690 --> 09:15.793
Saruwatari is suspected of murder.

183
09:17.862 --> 09:21.599
Saruwatari or Tabatake? Who handed him the water?

184
09:24.902 --> 09:28.305
Ms. Saruwatari, I have a spare bottle.

185
09:28.372 --> 09:30.107
Take it to Mr. Nikaido.

186
09:30.708 --> 09:31.609
Yes.

187
09:33.644 --> 09:35.513
What? Yes, like that.

188
09:37.848 --> 09:39.450
-Can you get it off? -Yes.

189
09:44.088 --> 09:47.825
So you say Saruwatari handed over Tabatake's water?

190
09:47.892 --> 09:50.861
Her testimony was consistent with the truth.

191
09:53.698 --> 09:56.233
Do you believe Tabatake intended to kill him?

192
09:57.368 --> 09:58.602
That's hard to say.

193
09:59.170 --> 10:01.172
Just tell us your subjective opinion.

194
10:05.342 --> 10:08.446
She didn't look like she was trying to kill him.

195
10:10.247 --> 10:13.751
This fact was never shared with our investigation team.

196
10:15.119 --> 10:16.253
You're right.

197
10:17.388 --> 10:20.357
Do you know what situation Saruwatari is in?

198
10:20.424 --> 10:23.227
Every day, she is accused of murder,

199
10:23.294 --> 10:26.097
she denies it, yet the police don't believe her at all!

200
10:27.431 --> 10:29.467
If you could testify in her favor…

201
10:29.533 --> 10:32.236
We can't share what we saw and learned

202
10:32.303 --> 10:35.940
with an unspecified number of investigators.

203
10:36.006 --> 10:38.809
Our investigation is secret within our own agencies.

204
10:38.876 --> 10:41.345
How can I prove Saruwatari's innocence?

205
10:41.412 --> 10:43.414
How many times do I have to say it?

206
10:44.215 --> 10:47.752
You live deep in the mountains, so you may not have seen or heard of it.

207
10:48.319 --> 10:51.088
Last year, a highly lethal drug

208
10:51.155 --> 10:55.359
was widely circulated in Sapporo, Hakodate, Tokyo, and Kanagawa.

209
10:56.761 --> 10:58.162
It goes by the name "CAN-d."

210
10:58.229 --> 11:00.464
Its addictiveness rivals fentanyl.

211
11:00.531 --> 11:02.933
Many users die of an overdose.

212
11:03.000 --> 11:05.336
They can't control their actions.

213
11:05.402 --> 11:07.338
What Tabatake carried

214
11:07.404 --> 11:09.940
was an ingredient used as a raw material for CAN-d.

215
11:10.007 --> 11:13.344
Before it is manufactured and circulated again,

216
11:13.410 --> 11:18.282
we must root it out at the source, or lives and futures will be ruined.

217
11:18.349 --> 11:19.550
That must not happen.

218
11:20.117 --> 11:22.620
Between Saruwatari, who is only suspected of murder,

219
11:22.686 --> 11:26.323
and the many people who will die if we fail,

220
11:27.391 --> 11:28.893
which matters more?

221
11:31.729 --> 11:35.800
It's not about who matters more or less!

222
11:38.769 --> 11:42.506
You are okay with letting an innocent person take the blame?

223
11:45.776 --> 11:50.214
If that's allowed, what are we police even for?

224
11:53.984 --> 11:57.855
I'm an amateur, so it's not my place to interrupt.

225
11:59.156 --> 12:02.026
But just being suspected of murder

226
12:03.127 --> 12:06.197
can ruin a person's life.

227
12:07.431 --> 12:09.500
Ms. Saruwatari is a teacher.

228
12:10.301 --> 12:14.705
Like all of you, her job requires trust, first and foremost.

229
12:14.772 --> 12:18.709
I ask that you show the slightest bit of decency.

230
12:22.580 --> 12:23.781
Please.

231
12:26.483 --> 12:27.585
I'll take you home.

232
12:27.651 --> 12:29.620
Could you answer my question?

233
12:29.687 --> 12:30.554
What?

234
12:31.455 --> 12:34.091
Where did Harune go?

235
12:39.997 --> 12:45.069
The fact that the three of you are in Tokyo…

236
12:45.970 --> 12:47.671
means you haven't found her yet.

237
12:47.738 --> 12:49.473
Or you're keeping her under surveillance.

238
12:50.341 --> 12:52.576
Two options. Which is it?

239
12:53.611 --> 12:58.082
Well, we have also gathered some information--

240
12:58.148 --> 12:59.083
That hurts!

241
12:59.149 --> 13:00.484
We don't need it.

242
13:01.418 --> 13:03.220
I haven't said anything yet!

243
13:05.289 --> 13:06.323
Sorry.

244
13:06.390 --> 13:07.858
Don't report what you've found.

245
13:08.926 --> 13:09.894
Undo the setting.

246
13:20.771 --> 13:22.806
Just quietly go back to your small town.

247
13:25.142 --> 13:25.976
Hey!

248
13:26.043 --> 13:28.445
You, take them out of here.

249
13:44.228 --> 13:45.496
You understand, right?

250
13:45.562 --> 13:48.766
We understand. We won't tell anyone. Right?

251
13:55.706 --> 13:57.708
Idiot!

252
13:57.775 --> 13:59.410
He can't hear you.

253
14:01.879 --> 14:02.947
Your flight back.

254
14:03.514 --> 14:04.548
Will you make it?

255
14:06.317 --> 14:07.651
I still have time.

256
14:09.553 --> 14:11.555
Then let's have coffee.

257
14:13.390 --> 14:15.225
Ogoma, you should try shouting it too.

258
14:15.292 --> 14:16.894
-Idiot! -Idiot!

259
14:17.895 --> 14:21.131
Again, I'm surprised how gutsy you are.

260
14:21.198 --> 14:23.534
You did well, sticking with me.

261
14:24.601 --> 14:28.539
I thought I would get kidnapped again. I was ready to die.

262
14:28.605 --> 14:29.807
Thank you for waiting.

263
14:29.873 --> 14:31.542
Thank you. Here.

264
14:31.608 --> 14:32.977
Thank you.

265
14:34.311 --> 14:37.414
If this is a contest, it feels like we've lost, right?

266
14:37.481 --> 14:40.884
Yes, we lost.

267
14:43.620 --> 14:46.623
But Ms. Aya's testimony wasn't a lie.

268
14:47.324 --> 14:51.362
You grasped the truth and also stood up for what's important.

269
14:51.428 --> 14:52.796
Not bad.

270
14:54.264 --> 14:55.432
Thanks.

271
14:56.867 --> 14:59.470
I couldn't ask even half the things I wanted.

272
15:00.437 --> 15:03.807
Why did Ms. Tabatake hand water to Nikaido, of all people?

273
15:07.044 --> 15:08.045
Let's…

274
15:09.246 --> 15:10.614
take a break from thinking.

275
15:13.784 --> 15:15.319
Ms. Tabatake…

276
15:15.386 --> 15:19.056
Maybe she didn't know about the sleeping pills in the bottle.

277
15:19.723 --> 15:21.658
Is that possible?

278
15:22.593 --> 15:23.494
Well…

279
15:23.560 --> 15:27.264
The customs man said he couldn't tell whether she had intent to kill.

280
15:27.331 --> 15:30.300
But the beneficiary on the hiking insurance was rewritten, right?

281
15:30.367 --> 15:32.970
Maybe she was trying to cast suspicion on Ms. Aya.

282
15:33.037 --> 15:35.773
I wonder.

283
15:37.274 --> 15:43.080
Maybe Ms. Tabatake thought Nikaido would harm her.

284
15:44.348 --> 15:48.118
If a tragedy happened on the mountain and the insurance looked suspicious,

285
15:48.185 --> 15:50.754
the police would start investigating.

286
15:52.256 --> 15:57.694
Maybe she rewrote the beneficiary's name as an SOS.

287
15:57.761 --> 15:59.797
You're really defending Tabatake.

288
16:01.398 --> 16:03.600
I think it's true she was a courier.

289
16:03.667 --> 16:07.204
But the Narcotics woman said she carried an ingredient.

290
16:07.905 --> 16:10.040
She didn't say she carried drugs.

291
16:11.341 --> 16:17.247
If what she carried wasn't illegal, we can't say she is a criminal.

292
16:17.314 --> 16:21.185
If she were a criminal, what happens to her life insurance money?

293
16:22.152 --> 16:23.887
I can't say anything for now.

294
16:23.954 --> 16:25.222
Say it.

295
16:27.391 --> 16:29.460
There are cases where it isn't paid.

296
16:33.931 --> 16:36.333
You want Nono to get it, right?

297
16:36.400 --> 16:38.402
No. I want to get my fee.

298
16:38.936 --> 16:42.573
If the insurance is paid, I get a commission.

299
16:44.708 --> 16:46.610
Do you really just want money?

300
16:48.879 --> 16:53.283
If she is only suspected, the life insurance should be paid in full.

301
16:53.851 --> 16:56.920
It's the policyholder's and beneficiary's right.

302
16:58.489 --> 17:02.459
It's sad for Nono, but a criminal is usually penalized.

303
17:02.526 --> 17:05.762
You say that because you're a police officer. I am--

304
17:05.829 --> 17:09.099
An insurance investigator, so you think in money.

305
17:11.235 --> 17:12.469
We don't…

306
17:12.536 --> 17:13.937
See things the same way.

307
17:19.343 --> 17:20.777
-I've got to go soon. -Okay.

308
17:21.345 --> 17:23.347
I'll stay a bit longer to look for Harune.

309
17:24.081 --> 17:25.082
Sure.

310
17:26.250 --> 17:28.685
Finally, I'll be free from this heat.

311
17:28.752 --> 17:31.555
I'll finally be free of you, Ogoma.

312
17:31.622 --> 17:33.023
That comeback is lame.

313
17:34.258 --> 17:35.859
Thanks for the coffee.

314
17:35.926 --> 17:36.927
Bye.

315
17:36.994 --> 17:38.128
Take care.

316
17:38.195 --> 17:39.196
I will.

317
17:55.479 --> 17:56.446
Hey! I'm back.

318
17:56.513 --> 17:57.814
It has been a while!

319
17:57.881 --> 17:58.749
Long time no see.

320
18:10.661 --> 18:11.495
Good morning.

321
18:11.562 --> 18:12.729
Welcome back!

322
18:12.796 --> 18:13.764
Here, souvenirs.

323
18:13.830 --> 18:15.365
How was your summer vacation?

324
18:15.432 --> 18:16.967
Did you enjoy Tokyo?

325
18:17.034 --> 18:19.269
I did…

326
18:19.336 --> 18:20.204
You got a girl there?

327
18:20.270 --> 18:21.972
No.

328
18:26.810 --> 18:30.013
Mr. Awashima, you really helped me out.

329
18:30.080 --> 18:31.315
They already found out.

330
18:31.381 --> 18:32.482
Ogoma!

331
18:33.183 --> 18:35.419
Go quickly. Hurry!

332
18:37.020 --> 18:38.288
Did you really enjoy Tokyo?

333
18:42.326 --> 18:43.260
Okay.

334
18:46.163 --> 18:48.065
Excuse me.

335
18:48.765 --> 18:51.068
Headquarters gave a strict warning.

336
18:51.868 --> 18:55.439
They said you chased Harune and obstructed another team's investigation.

337
18:56.540 --> 19:00.677
Chief, did you already know about those people's investigation?

338
19:02.045 --> 19:05.782
We were ordered not to go after the three missing people.

339
19:06.950 --> 19:11.989
It involved a secret investigation, and we were told not to butt in.

340
19:12.055 --> 19:12.889
I see.

341
19:12.956 --> 19:15.392
Read the Investigation Rules properly!

342
19:15.926 --> 19:19.863
In conducting an investigation, do not go off on your own!

343
19:19.930 --> 19:21.798
Obey your superiors' orders!

344
19:21.865 --> 19:22.933
I'm sorry!

345
19:23.467 --> 19:25.969
Oh, and about Nikaido.

346
19:26.703 --> 19:29.039
Saruwatari is no longer a suspect.

347
19:33.010 --> 19:34.177
Really?

348
19:34.244 --> 19:37.848
New testimony came out, so the investigation changed direction.

349
19:37.914 --> 19:41.585
The team whose investigation you obstructed provided statements.

350
19:44.621 --> 19:45.856
Then…

351
19:46.456 --> 19:48.825
is the suspect now Tabatake?

352
19:49.693 --> 19:52.763
It's not a solo job. HQ thinks there's a ringleader.

353
19:53.563 --> 19:54.464
A ringleader?

354
19:54.531 --> 19:58.268
They're starting to identify who is behind all of this.

355
20:03.373 --> 20:06.076
They told you to return to the investigation this Thursday!

356
20:07.244 --> 20:08.345
Yes, sir!

357
20:12.549 --> 20:13.817
Hello, miss.

358
20:15.085 --> 20:16.019
Huh?

359
20:17.287 --> 20:18.121
Excuse me.

360
20:18.722 --> 20:20.223
-Yes? -Where is Ms. Saruwatari?

361
20:20.290 --> 20:22.059
Oh, she was discharged.

362
20:22.125 --> 20:23.860
-When? -Earlier today.

363
20:23.927 --> 20:25.595
Got it. Thank you.

364
20:30.300 --> 20:32.135
I see you were discharged.

365
20:32.202 --> 20:33.270
I'm glad.

366
20:38.208 --> 20:40.243
Can we meet tomorrow?

367
20:45.082 --> 20:47.451
WE CAN. I NEED TO GO SOMEWHERE…

368
20:47.517 --> 20:49.319
LIFE INSURANCE CONTRACT TERUYUKI NIKAIDO

369
20:49.386 --> 20:50.487
Time is up.

370
20:50.554 --> 20:53.023
We must submit this report to the insurance company.

371
20:53.090 --> 20:56.660
Let's wait for them to tell us whether to continue looking for Harune.

372
20:56.727 --> 20:59.262
-How many days must I wait-- -I'll submit the report.

373
20:59.329 --> 21:00.464
Thanks for the hard work.

374
21:00.530 --> 21:01.331
FINISHED

375
21:03.934 --> 21:05.902
Did you find the person you were looking for?

376
21:06.503 --> 21:08.505
Well, Ogoma found his.

377
21:08.572 --> 21:12.008
I'm heading back to Hokkaido to regroup.

378
21:12.676 --> 21:13.844
So you didn't find yours.

379
21:14.544 --> 21:15.879
Unfortunately not.

380
21:25.155 --> 21:28.425
Do you know what this is?

381
21:30.260 --> 21:31.895
I looked into lots of things, but…

382
21:33.130 --> 21:34.231
Where did you find it?

383
21:34.297 --> 21:36.099
It was found in someone's postbox.

384
21:37.434 --> 21:38.335
How about this?

385
21:38.902 --> 21:40.404
That's only seven digits, though.

386
21:40.470 --> 21:44.074
This is a digital address that tells you even the apartment number.

387
21:45.208 --> 21:46.977
Our company uses it often.

388
21:47.711 --> 21:49.212
There, okay…

389
21:49.279 --> 21:50.614
An address?

390
21:51.148 --> 21:53.417
-What about the last four digits-- -An address.

391
21:54.151 --> 21:56.420
HOSHIMINO HEIGHTS 307 AOMINE WARD, YOKOHAMA, KANAGAWA

392
22:02.192 --> 22:03.493
Sorry to call you here--

393
22:03.560 --> 22:05.829
Hoshimino 4-3-12, we've arrived.

394
22:06.863 --> 22:08.198
You should have told me earlier!

395
22:08.265 --> 22:11.535
Look, we weren't on good terms earlier.

396
22:12.169 --> 22:13.036
Is it here?

397
22:13.103 --> 22:14.838
Who lives here?

398
22:14.905 --> 22:15.939
An illegal sublet.

399
22:16.006 --> 22:17.474
They take guests without registering.

400
22:17.541 --> 22:18.708
Sublet?

401
22:18.775 --> 22:22.412
-What's the apartment number? -It's 307.

402
22:31.655 --> 22:33.290
The last four digits.

403
22:35.091 --> 22:37.160
Nine, four, seven, one.

404
22:39.763 --> 22:40.797
Hey!

405
22:41.398 --> 22:42.466
Wait!

406
22:42.532 --> 22:43.633
I don't know anything!

407
22:43.700 --> 22:46.403
I'm just a part-timer! They hired me as a courier!

408
22:48.538 --> 22:49.539
Here?

409
22:53.109 --> 22:54.344
Contact Narcotics.

410
22:54.411 --> 22:55.378
Okay.

411
22:57.147 --> 22:58.782
Excuse me.

412
22:59.416 --> 23:00.750
Stay there.

413
23:01.284 --> 23:02.319
Don't come in.

414
23:02.385 --> 23:03.353
Okay.

415
23:07.190 --> 23:08.925
Something has been bugging me.

416
23:11.061 --> 23:13.063
I'm older than you, right?

417
23:21.137 --> 23:23.373
-So what? -Nothing.

418
23:24.508 --> 23:26.142
Hello. Sorry to bother you.

419
23:26.209 --> 23:27.077
I'm just a part-timer!

420
23:27.143 --> 23:30.747
It seems they changed locations for each deal, with digital addresses.

421
23:30.814 --> 23:31.715
I'll request backup.

422
23:37.020 --> 23:38.455
Should I help?

423
23:46.730 --> 23:48.498
-Hold this. -Okay.

424
23:52.569 --> 23:53.637
Light up where I'm looking!

425
23:53.703 --> 23:56.172
Yes, sorry. Here.

426
23:57.507 --> 23:58.408
Whoa.

427
23:59.342 --> 24:00.911
That Shikara cop…

428
24:02.012 --> 24:03.246
You mean Ogoma?

429
24:03.313 --> 24:04.481
What kind of guy is he?

430
24:05.081 --> 24:06.917
That's a hard question to answer.

431
24:07.584 --> 24:09.019
His strengths and weaknesses?

432
24:10.620 --> 24:13.557
His strength lies in his persistence.

433
24:14.157 --> 24:15.825
Rather than shallow justice,

434
24:15.892 --> 24:18.128
it's a better quality for detectives to have.

435
24:18.194 --> 24:19.229
His weakness?

436
24:19.763 --> 24:21.498
He's frighteningly impulsive.

437
24:21.565 --> 24:25.468
But with a good boss, he'll grow. Probably.

438
24:36.880 --> 24:38.748
Send a Forensics team here.

439
24:41.051 --> 24:42.719
What money is this?

440
24:43.954 --> 24:46.923
If I learn where Harune went, I'll tell you.

441
24:46.990 --> 24:48.091
Really?

442
24:50.026 --> 24:51.861
Go back to that small town.

443
24:53.330 --> 24:54.297
Okay.

444
25:02.672 --> 25:05.508
The police stopped calling me.

445
25:05.575 --> 25:08.144
It's all thanks to you, Ogoma. Thank you.

446
25:08.678 --> 25:11.648
You sure you don't mind coming with me here?

447
25:11.715 --> 25:12.649
It's fine.

448
25:13.216 --> 25:15.518
I'm from this town too.

449
25:15.585 --> 25:16.920
Trainee teachers like me

450
25:16.987 --> 25:19.990
usually teach at the very school they graduated from.

451
25:20.056 --> 25:22.959
Huh? So we went to the same middle school?

452
25:23.026 --> 25:25.929
Was your friend at the same school too?

453
25:26.463 --> 25:28.131
Yes. He was three years older.

454
25:28.198 --> 25:31.001
And our houses were next to each other.

455
25:32.202 --> 25:34.971
Do you come here to pay respects every year?

456
25:38.408 --> 25:39.309
Tetsu!

457
25:40.143 --> 25:41.044
I'm here!

458
25:41.711 --> 25:44.014
Hey, Tetsu, please! Wake up!

459
25:44.581 --> 25:46.182
Please, don't die!

460
25:47.283 --> 25:48.918
Don't die!

461
25:50.153 --> 25:51.221
Please!

462
25:53.289 --> 25:54.357
Don't die…

463
25:55.492 --> 25:59.696
My parents weren't around often.

464
26:01.464 --> 26:05.468
Whenever I got home, the house was always dark and empty.

465
26:07.303 --> 26:08.204
So,

466
26:09.506 --> 26:12.075
Tetsu always told me to come to his house.

467
26:14.377 --> 26:16.579
I basically lived there.

468
26:21.017 --> 26:24.621
I would eat meals at his place.

469
26:28.358 --> 26:30.560
Slept on a futon at his place.

470
26:32.228 --> 26:34.030
He wasn't a friend anymore.

471
26:34.097 --> 26:35.465
He was basically family to you.

472
26:40.303 --> 26:44.674
I probably talked with Tetsu more than I talked to my parents.

473
26:47.410 --> 26:51.581
We only ever talked about dumb stuff though.

474
26:57.153 --> 27:02.158
If an adult like you had come into our lives earlier…

475
27:07.530 --> 27:10.333
maybe Tetsu would still be alive.

476
27:16.239 --> 27:20.176
I wasn't really an adult either.

477
27:21.211 --> 27:22.512
I was still in university.

478
27:25.815 --> 27:27.784
You looked like an adult to me.

479
27:28.818 --> 27:30.186
I'll come back, Tetsu.

480
27:32.856 --> 27:36.993
I wasn't even sure if I could be a teacher.

481
27:37.927 --> 27:40.964
Last year, the school closed down. Did you know that?

482
27:41.030 --> 27:41.898
What?

483
27:41.965 --> 27:45.235
Not enough kids in town anymore.

484
27:45.301 --> 27:46.836
Even in my time, there weren't many.

485
27:46.903 --> 27:47.737
Ogoma.

486
27:47.804 --> 27:48.872
When I climb mountains,

487
27:48.938 --> 27:52.242
I sometimes meet kids whom I taught back then.

488
27:52.308 --> 27:56.079
They say the school hike inspired them to start climbing.

489
27:57.313 --> 27:59.382
So school events do have meaning.

490
27:59.449 --> 28:00.884
Of course they do.

491
28:00.950 --> 28:02.185
I always skipped them.

492
28:02.252 --> 28:03.353
Do you even go to work?

493
28:03.419 --> 28:04.721
I skip it too…

494
28:05.321 --> 28:09.292
I know. Someday you'll be a legendary cop.

495
28:09.359 --> 28:10.927
Do you mean that in a good way?

496
28:10.994 --> 28:12.095
Of course.

497
28:15.131 --> 28:16.399
Brings back memories, huh?

498
28:16.466 --> 28:18.568
It sure does.

499
28:20.603 --> 28:22.105
It's hot.

500
28:22.172 --> 28:23.006
Yes.

501
28:24.507 --> 28:25.341
This is my seat.

502
28:31.848 --> 28:32.515
Ogoma.

503
28:33.349 --> 28:35.919
I need you to help me with something after school.

504
28:40.657 --> 28:41.558
What?

505
28:44.494 --> 28:45.862
I have a problem.

506
28:46.729 --> 28:47.664
Yeah?

507
28:49.299 --> 28:52.302
Seeing dead bodies really takes a toll on me.

508
28:54.938 --> 28:57.674
-Sorry for talking about this. -It's fine.

509
28:58.842 --> 28:59.776
May I continue?

510
29:00.310 --> 29:01.344
Of course.

511
29:02.545 --> 29:04.914
I was assigned to the criminal section.

512
29:05.415 --> 29:08.618
It investigates murders and robberies.

513
29:10.420 --> 29:13.756
But my jurisdiction is peaceful. Basically zero murders.

514
29:14.524 --> 29:18.628
Sometimes, elderly people die of old age, but experienced officers handle it.

515
29:19.495 --> 29:22.932
This case was my first time at a scene.

516
29:26.269 --> 29:30.840
Can someone like me ever become a legendary cop?

517
29:36.613 --> 29:41.351
Back then, you could have run away.

518
29:42.385 --> 29:46.122
To avoid being involved, you could have pretended not to know anything.

519
29:48.424 --> 29:49.459
But…

520
29:50.393 --> 29:52.395
you chose not to run away.

521
29:53.062 --> 29:57.066
You called an ambulance and tried to save Tetsu.

522
29:59.569 --> 30:02.505
Don't think that you could have done more.

523
30:06.342 --> 30:09.312
You did everything you could.

524
30:11.080 --> 30:12.715
You did the right thing.

525
30:31.968 --> 30:35.271
If one of your students is involved in anything dangerous, please tell me.

526
30:36.372 --> 30:39.008
I'll do my best to stop them.

527
30:43.346 --> 30:46.582
My students are all good kids.

528
30:47.083 --> 30:51.888
But if one of them ever becomes like that, please help me out.

529
30:52.989 --> 30:54.057
Yes.

530
30:55.291 --> 30:56.326
I'm counting on you.

531
30:57.060 --> 30:58.161
Leave it to me.

532
30:59.462 --> 31:01.197
Pass the shuttlecock!

533
31:01.264 --> 31:02.699
Yes!

534
31:02.765 --> 31:04.233
Focus!

535
31:05.234 --> 31:06.536
Make them all count!

536
31:07.103 --> 31:09.539
Tomorrow, five reps, ten sets.

537
31:09.605 --> 31:10.873
What?

538
31:10.940 --> 31:12.008
Don't "what" me.

539
31:12.075 --> 31:14.877
I'll increase it to ten reps, ten sets, you know.

540
31:15.778 --> 31:17.814
That's when you should go, "what"!

541
31:19.148 --> 31:20.516
Thank you very much.

542
31:21.217 --> 31:23.252
Thank you very much.

543
31:23.319 --> 31:24.387
Tidy up!

544
31:24.454 --> 31:25.621
Yes!

545
31:30.126 --> 31:31.527
Ms. Saruwatari.

546
31:32.495 --> 31:34.430
I need your advice on something.

547
31:36.032 --> 31:37.867
It was found in our club room.

548
31:37.934 --> 31:40.670
A second-year picked it up and brought it in.

549
31:41.738 --> 31:44.407
None of the club members recognize it.

550
31:46.242 --> 31:49.178
We got a notice last year from the Board of Education, right?

551
31:49.245 --> 31:50.246
Yes.

552
31:50.313 --> 31:52.448
They were warning us about a drug.

553
31:52.515 --> 31:54.384
SAMPLE PHOTO

554
31:54.450 --> 31:55.818
"CAN-d."

555
31:58.054 --> 31:59.789
Have you told the principal?

556
31:59.856 --> 32:02.525
Yes, but he hasn't answered yet.

557
32:03.159 --> 32:05.661
The club members are suspecting each other,

558
32:05.728 --> 32:06.596
and things are tense.

559
32:06.662 --> 32:07.730
Calm down.

560
32:07.797 --> 32:09.365
Maybe this is just a supplement.

561
32:09.432 --> 32:10.933
What should we do?

562
32:14.771 --> 32:17.006
I'll try a component analysis.

563
32:17.073 --> 32:20.076
Until the result comes out, don't blame anyone.

564
32:20.143 --> 32:21.778
You can have it analyzed?

565
32:23.646 --> 32:26.382
I know someone who can.

566
32:35.892 --> 32:37.527
OGOMA - SHIKARA STATION

567
32:49.238 --> 32:52.942
Huh? Are you going somewhere? Want to go together?

568
32:54.110 --> 32:56.913
You go ahead first. You have a flight, right?

569
32:59.282 --> 33:02.685
Oh, thank you for helping me with that digital address.

570
33:05.888 --> 33:07.957
See you. And thanks again.

571
33:15.465 --> 33:16.399
Yes?

572
33:16.466 --> 33:18.401
Hello! You have a parcel!

573
33:18.468 --> 33:19.902
Please wait a bit.

574
33:21.237 --> 33:22.171
Oh, sorry!

575
33:22.238 --> 33:23.673
It's heavy, please be careful.

576
33:23.739 --> 33:24.974
Okay.

577
33:25.541 --> 33:26.409
Yes.

578
33:26.943 --> 33:28.177
Sorry, Akane, may I?

579
33:28.244 --> 33:29.112
Sure.

580
33:29.946 --> 33:31.614
It's from Ogoma.

581
33:44.494 --> 33:46.429
Wow!

582
33:47.029 --> 33:48.397
Huh?

583
33:49.165 --> 33:50.867
Amazing.

584
33:51.567 --> 33:53.636
How do you even eat this?

585
33:53.703 --> 33:55.471
You plan to eat it alone?

586
33:56.506 --> 33:59.142
He sent it to both you and me.

587
34:00.309 --> 34:01.878
But you're leaving, right?

588
34:03.713 --> 34:05.781
I'll change to another flight.

589
34:07.083 --> 34:09.385
Is this for a paella?

590
34:10.019 --> 34:13.890
What are you saying? I'm sure you grill this with salt and butter.

591
34:13.956 --> 34:14.924
What?

592
34:21.597 --> 34:22.698
Have you been already?

593
34:22.765 --> 34:23.599
What?

594
34:24.433 --> 34:25.935
To Minori's grave.

595
34:26.869 --> 34:28.471
I plan to go now.

596
34:30.373 --> 34:31.307
I see.

597
34:36.979 --> 34:38.414
Maybe I'll go too.

598
34:46.689 --> 34:50.059
When you come back, let's talk a bit.

599
34:50.860 --> 34:52.762
About what we do from now on.

600
34:54.230 --> 34:55.831
Will you come back to me,

601
34:56.732 --> 34:58.334
or do we keep living separately?

602
35:02.071 --> 35:03.005
Sure.

603
35:04.607 --> 35:05.708
Let's do that.

604
35:27.330 --> 35:29.232
Which do you want to eat first?

605
35:32.301 --> 35:33.269
Scallops?

606
35:41.544 --> 35:44.146
-Welcome. Please wait there. -Hello. Okay!

607
35:51.153 --> 35:52.421
You're that missing person!

608
35:52.488 --> 35:55.558
Cut it out already.

609
35:56.259 --> 35:57.860
How long have you been here?

610
35:57.927 --> 35:59.128
-Excuse me. -Yes?

611
35:59.195 --> 36:02.365
-I'm Nobori. I have a reservation. -Mr. Nobori, I'll show you to your seat.

612
36:02.431 --> 36:03.266
Okay.

613
36:04.066 --> 36:05.201
Hey!

614
36:07.670 --> 36:08.638
Are you a kid?

615
36:09.639 --> 36:10.473
You drove here?

616
36:10.539 --> 36:12.775
Why would I? We're going to drink, right?

617
36:12.842 --> 36:13.876
Go ahead then.

618
36:13.943 --> 36:16.312
Sorry I couldn't go on the cleaning trek.

619
36:16.912 --> 36:19.682
Everyone was saying it's rare for you to miss a trip.

620
36:19.749 --> 36:23.185
It's really pathetic. I got careless.

621
36:23.252 --> 36:24.720
-Thank you. -Looks good.

622
36:25.321 --> 36:26.789
What are you getting?

623
36:29.191 --> 36:30.192
Napolitan pasta.

624
36:30.259 --> 36:34.330
I get it. I'm torn between curry and the Napolitan.

625
36:34.397 --> 36:37.266
I don't know which to pick. Which one?

626
36:37.333 --> 36:38.301
I'll give you half.

627
36:38.367 --> 36:40.102
Really? Then I'll take it.

628
36:40.169 --> 36:42.271
-One Napolitan and one curry. -Yes.

629
36:42.338 --> 36:44.040
-Yes, and two beers. -Yes.

630
36:44.106 --> 36:45.875
-Thank you. -Coming right up.

631
36:47.443 --> 36:48.377
So…

632
36:50.780 --> 36:52.548
Will we talk first?

633
36:52.615 --> 36:55.284
-Or after the meal? -Let's talk first.

634
36:56.185 --> 36:57.186
Okay.

635
36:59.021 --> 37:02.191
Can you keep this a secret?

636
37:04.293 --> 37:05.328
What's wrong?

637
37:08.164 --> 37:09.198
What?

638
37:19.375 --> 37:20.343
This.

639
37:20.910 --> 37:22.878
I want to know what this is.

640
37:24.380 --> 37:25.381
What is it?

641
37:27.983 --> 37:28.951
Huh?

642
37:30.286 --> 37:31.354
Keep it there.

643
37:33.356 --> 37:35.124
That's what I want to find out.

644
37:37.093 --> 37:39.061
-Can I open it? -Yes.

645
37:44.400 --> 37:48.070
No matter the results, you mustn't tell anyone but me.

646
37:51.507 --> 37:52.942
Welcome back.

647
37:53.509 --> 37:55.511
Huh? Got a new look?

648
37:56.045 --> 37:57.079
Thanks.

649
37:58.047 --> 38:00.783
The seafood you sent was great. Especially the scallops.

650
38:01.417 --> 38:02.585
They were sent fresh that morning.

651
38:02.651 --> 38:07.156
Akane and I ate our fill.

652
38:15.731 --> 38:18.401
I'm glad Akane liked it.

653
38:19.735 --> 38:22.371
Oh, what about Harune?

654
38:23.606 --> 38:25.541
I haven't found her.

655
38:26.041 --> 38:28.010
Then why did you come back?

656
38:28.077 --> 38:31.147
Time ran out, I had to submit the report.

657
38:31.213 --> 38:32.915
And I want to help with Nono's matter.

658
38:38.721 --> 38:42.191
Anyway, I got an appointment with Dr. Yoshino.

659
38:42.258 --> 38:43.826
Ogoma, want to come with me?

660
38:44.727 --> 38:47.263
The chief told me not to do any unnecessary investigating.

661
38:47.830 --> 38:50.766
Maybe we can learn Ms. Tabatake's cash flow.

662
38:51.534 --> 38:53.202
Is that unnecessary?

663
38:54.170 --> 38:58.674
I think the one in the wrong here is the police, not you.

664
39:04.747 --> 39:06.282
Let's go talk to him.

665
39:07.383 --> 39:09.118
Sorry to keep you waiting. I've been busy.

666
39:09.185 --> 39:12.455
We came to talk to you on behalf of Chika.

667
39:12.521 --> 39:14.490
Here's the consent form.

668
39:14.557 --> 39:16.325
It's about Nono's medical costs, right?

669
39:17.126 --> 39:18.761
Chika called me this morning.

670
39:19.862 --> 39:21.864
You mind if I eat while we talk?

671
39:21.931 --> 39:24.934
Of course not. Sorry for bothering you.

672
39:28.404 --> 39:32.074
Ms. Tabatake's death was truly regrettable.

673
39:35.211 --> 39:36.946
How is Nono?

674
39:37.012 --> 39:38.747
She still has a low fever.

675
39:38.814 --> 39:42.518
Her illness? I heard gene therapy might help.

676
39:42.585 --> 39:45.754
As pretreatment, we're giving her chemotherapy drugs.

677
39:46.288 --> 39:48.257
The therapy can be quite taxing.

678
39:50.926 --> 39:56.565
Chika gave us this. Nono's medical costs are listed here.

679
39:56.632 --> 39:58.968
They're quite high.

680
39:59.034 --> 40:02.104
Some months cost over a million yen.

681
40:02.171 --> 40:05.274
Is this correct?

682
40:05.341 --> 40:06.408
It is.

683
40:07.877 --> 40:09.912
Why does it cost this much?

684
40:09.979 --> 40:13.315
The medicine prescribed for her is unapproved in Japan,

685
40:14.049 --> 40:15.417
so it's out-of-pocket.

686
40:16.352 --> 40:18.020
Insurance doesn't apply.

687
40:19.388 --> 40:22.291
Conventional medication had no effect on her anymore.

688
40:23.492 --> 40:25.394
So you have to use this drug?

689
40:27.129 --> 40:32.268
It costs more than 600,000 yen a month.

690
40:32.334 --> 40:34.069
Each case is different.

691
40:34.136 --> 40:37.039
But in this specific case, prescribing a non-insured drug

692
40:37.573 --> 40:40.175
makes other medical fees out-of-pocket too. All of it.

693
40:41.377 --> 40:43.445
Subsidy programs can't be used either.

694
40:45.214 --> 40:49.518
Do you know how Ms. Tabatake paid this astronomical amount?

695
40:50.286 --> 40:51.420
No.

696
40:51.487 --> 40:53.889
A normal person can't earn this much a month.

697
40:54.423 --> 40:58.561
For Nono's comfort, Ms. Tabatake chose this drug for the treatment.

698
41:00.296 --> 41:04.199
If the family can afford it, we doctors will respect their wishes.

699
41:04.833 --> 41:08.671
What happens with Nono's medication from now on?

700
41:09.772 --> 41:12.341
Chika said it will be paid from Ms. Tabatake's savings.

701
41:14.510 --> 41:16.779
Do you know how much her savings are?

702
41:21.884 --> 41:23.719
They won't last six months.

703
41:23.786 --> 41:25.554
At most, four months.

704
41:26.088 --> 41:28.357
Only four months, I see.

705
41:28.924 --> 41:33.095
If Ms. Tabatake's life insurance is paid, they can manage.

706
41:33.762 --> 41:36.932
They can buy time until gene therapy is possible.

707
41:36.999 --> 41:39.201
But Ms. Tabatake is surely guilty.

708
41:39.768 --> 41:42.671
Her motive for needing money is clear.

709
41:42.738 --> 41:44.807
You can't be certain she is guilty yet!

710
41:44.873 --> 41:47.209
We also don't know why she killed herself.

711
41:49.612 --> 41:51.547
Don't take crime lightly.

712
41:52.081 --> 41:54.450
Once an ordinary person commits a crime, in the end--

713
41:54.516 --> 41:56.452
Don't keep saying "crime this, crime that."

714
41:56.986 --> 42:01.023
When Ms. Aya was wrongly suspected, you were so angry.

715
42:01.890 --> 42:03.325
What's your problem?!

716
42:05.327 --> 42:08.063
You are doing all this for Nono, right?

717
42:08.864 --> 42:10.265
I just want the money.

718
42:14.470 --> 42:16.005
I won't give up.

719
42:17.139 --> 42:21.310
I'll do everything I can so that the life insurance can be paid.

720
42:22.044 --> 42:25.047
Even if the chance is 0.00001%.

721
42:27.049 --> 42:29.151
You're not thinking of doing something shady, are you?

722
42:29.218 --> 42:30.252
Shady?

723
42:30.319 --> 42:31.186
Yes.

724
42:31.787 --> 42:33.722
"Anything you can." What is that?

725
42:33.789 --> 42:35.357
Something illegal?

726
42:36.358 --> 42:38.460
No way.

727
42:38.527 --> 42:39.628
Really?

728
42:50.539 --> 42:52.274
I'll listen to your breathing.

729
42:56.578 --> 42:57.913
I'm going to check your eyes.

730
42:59.481 --> 43:00.916
I'm going to give her oxygen.

731
43:01.550 --> 43:02.985
I'm going to give you oxygen, okay?

732
43:03.519 --> 43:04.853
You'll feel better soon.

733
43:08.857 --> 43:10.125
Hang in there.

734
43:11.960 --> 43:13.062
Hang in there.

735
43:19.234 --> 43:20.169
You have a delivery!

736
43:20.235 --> 43:21.470
Oh, thank you.

737
43:21.537 --> 43:22.805
What is it?

738
43:22.871 --> 43:24.707
This is for Mommy.

739
43:24.773 --> 43:26.208
Let me open it!

740
43:26.275 --> 43:27.843
Be careful.

741
43:29.344 --> 43:30.412
Here you go!

742
43:30.479 --> 43:31.480
Thank you.

743
43:31.547 --> 43:32.681
And this too.

744
43:32.748 --> 43:33.682
Thanks.

745
43:33.749 --> 43:36.118
Thank you for your call. I'm Shimizu.

746
43:36.185 --> 43:38.854
Is this notebook my sister's?

747
43:39.488 --> 43:40.723
We believe so.

748
43:41.323 --> 43:42.925
Nono said it was her mom's.

749
43:43.992 --> 43:47.362
LIFE INSURANCE CONTRACT

750
43:55.404 --> 43:56.739
About the notebook…

751
43:56.805 --> 43:58.640
Please don't tell anyone about it.

752
43:58.707 --> 44:00.175
You hiding something from me?

753
44:00.242 --> 44:02.578
-You should consult the police. -Hey!

754
44:02.644 --> 44:04.480
Stay with me! Ogoma!

755
44:04.546 --> 44:05.514
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
